<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01LB">Notation <span data-tag="01LB">4.6.7.1</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a simplicial set. We define a simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]$ as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]$ has exactly two objects, which we will denote by $x$ and $y$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The morphism spaces in $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]$ are given by the formulae 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]}( x, x)_{\bullet } = \{  \operatorname{id}_{x} \}  \quad \quad \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]}(y,y)_{\bullet } = \{  \operatorname{id}_ y \}  \]
</div>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]}(x,y)_{\bullet } = K \quad \quad \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[K]}( y,x)_{\bullet } = \emptyset . \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
